uppercase\",\"color\":\"#F15D22\",\"marginBottom\":\"6px\"},\"children\":\"TL;DR\"}],\"A meter (symbol $\\\\mathrm{m}$) is the SI base unit of length — the international standard for measuring distance — equal to $100$ centimetres, $1000$ millimetres, and approximately $3.281$ feet. This article gives the formal definition, the metric prefix ladder, conversion to imperial units, three worked examples, and the most common conversion mistakes.\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"display\":\"flex\",\"alignItems\":\"center\",\"gap\":\"6px\",\"flexWrap\":\"wrap\",\"fontSize\":\"13px\",\"color\":\"#6B7280\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"width\":\"28px\",\"height\":\"28px\",\"borderRadius\":\"50%\",\"background\":\"linear-gradient(135deg,#F15D22,#FFB347)\",\"display\":\"flex\",\"alignItems\":\"center\",\"justifyContent\":\"center\",\"fontWeight\":800,\"fontSize\":\"10px\",\"color\":\"#fff\",\"flexShrink\":0},\"children\":\"BT\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/authors/bhanzu-team\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#F15D22\",\"fontWeight\":600,\"textDecoration\":\"none\"},\"children\":\"Bhanzu Team\"}],\"\",null,[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"width\":\"1px\",\"height\":\"14px\",\"background\":\"#DEE2E6\",\"margin\":\"0 6px\",\"display\":\"inline-block\"}}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Last updated on \",\"June 5, 2026\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"width\":\"1px\",\"height\":\"14px\",\"background\":\"#DEE2E6\",\"margin\":\"0 6px\",\"display\":\"inline-block\"}}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[8,\" min read\"]}]]}],\"\"]}],[\"$\",\"aside\",null,{\"className\":\"page-toc-aside\",\"style\":{\"gridColumn\":1,\"gridRow\":\"1 / span 2\",\"position\":\"sticky\",\"top\":\"120px\",\"alignSelf\":\"start\",\"display\":\"flex\",\"flexDirection\":\"column\",\"gap\":0,\"zIndex\":1},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L21\",null,{\"entries\":[{\"id\":\"the-formal-definition\",\"text\":\"The Formal Definition\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"the-metric-length-ladder-prefixes-and-powers-of-10\",\"text\":\"The Metric Length Ladder — Prefixes and Powers of 10\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"meter-to-imperial-the-most-used-conversions\",\"text\":\"Meter to Imperial — The Most-Used Conversions\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"three-worked-examples-of-meter-quick-standard-stretch\",\"text\":\"Three Worked Examples of Meter — Quick, Standard, Stretch\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"where-the-meter-appears-beyond-the-tape-measure\",\"text\":\"Where the Meter Appears — Beyond the Tape Measure\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"tripping-points-to-avoid-in-meter\",\"text\":\"Tripping Points to Avoid In Meter\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"conclusion\",\"text\":\"Conclusion\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"quick-self-check-three-conversions\",\"text\":\"Quick Self-Check — Three Conversions\",\"level\":2}],\"title\":\"Table of Contents\",\"activeColor\":\"#FF6B2B\",\"activeTextColor\":\"#0F1F3D\"}],\"$L22\",\"$L23\"]}],\"$L24\",\"$L25\"]}]}],\"$L26\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"18:[\"$\",\"$L27\",null,{\"text\":\"Book a FREE Demo Class\",\"ctaText\":\"Book Now →\",\"ctaUrl\":\"https://bhanzu.com/embeddable-demo-form?utm_source=blog-mobile\"}]\n19:[\"$\",\"$L28\",null,{}]\n1a:[\"$\",\"$L29\",null,{}]\n1b:[\"$\",\"$L2a\",null,{\"katex\":true,\"mermaid\":false}]\n2b:T3ea7,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\n        /* ── Page-level classes (overrideable by custom/template CSS) ── */\n        /* overflow-x:clip clips without creating a block formatting context,\n           so position:sticky still works on nav, TOC, and sidebar descendants.\n           (overflow:hidden would break sticky — that was the previous bug.) */\n        .page-root { background: #fff; color: #374151; overflow-x: clip; width: 100%; }\n        .page-hero { background: #fff; }\n        /* ── Featured image — LCP + CLS (Medium/Substack pattern) ───────────────\n           Lives inside the article header column, below the meta bar.\n           aspect-ratio:16/9 reserves exact space before bytes arrive → zero CLS.\n           border-radius keeps it within the article column as a designed element,\n           not a raw full-bleed banner. margin-top separates it from the meta bar.\n           fetchPriority=\"high\" on the \u003cimg\u003e makes it the LCP candidate without\n           the image having to dominate the entire above-the-fold viewport. */\n        .page-hero-img-wrap {\n          position: relative;\n          width: 100%;\n          aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          border-radius: 12px;\n          background: #F3F4F6;\n          margin-top: 20px;\n        }\n        .page-hero-img {\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          object-fit: cover;\n          display: block;\n        }\n        /* Grid container box-sizing so padding doesn't push it past viewport width */\n        .page-grid { box-sizing: border-box; width: 100%; }\n        .bhanzu-prose h1 { font-family: 'Quicksand','Quicksand Fallback',sans-serif; font-size: 28px; font-weight: 900; color: #0F1F3D; margin: 0 0 16px; line-height: 1.2; }\n        .bhanzu-prose h2 { font-family: 'Quicksand','Quicksand Fallback',sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 800; color: #0F1F3D; margin: 1.8em 0 0.35em; }\n        .bhanzu-prose h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }\n        .bhanzu-prose h3 { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; color: #0F1F3D; margin: 1.4em 0 0.25em; }\n        .bhanzu-prose h4 { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: #0F1F3D; margin: 18px 0 8px; }\n        /* max-width prevents the prose container itself from overflowing */\n        .bhanzu-prose { max-width: 100%; }\n        /* word-break + overflow-wrap only on flowing text — NOT inherited by tables */\n        .bhanzu-prose p, .bhanzu-prose li, .bhanzu-prose blockquote,\n        .bhanzu-prose h1, .bhanzu-prose h2, .bhanzu-prose h3, .bhanzu-prose h4 { word-break: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word; }\n        /* Hard reset on every table descendant — TipTap wraps \u003ctd\u003e content in \u003cp\u003e, so\n           targeting td alone is not enough; the inner \u003cp\u003e match above would still win.\n           !important ensures this beats any inherited or element-level override. */\n        .bhanzu-prose table, .bhanzu-prose table * { word-break: normal !important; overflow-wrap: normal !important; }\n        .bhanzu-prose p { font-size: 15px; color: #4B5563; margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.85; }\n        .bhanzu-prose strong { color: #0F1F3D; }\n        .bhanzu-prose em { font-style: italic; }\n        .bhanzu-prose a.md-link { color: #F15D22; font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 1px dotted rgba(255,107,43,.4); text-decoration: none; }\n        .bhanzu-prose a.md-link:hover { border-bottom-style: solid; }\n        /* ── Lists: fix bullet/number visibility ── */\n        .bhanzu-prose ul { padding-left: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; color: #4B5563; list-style-type: disc !important; }\n        .bhanzu-prose ol { padding-left: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; color: #4B5563; list-style-type: decimal !important; }\n        .bhanzu-prose li { margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 15px; display: list-item !important; }\n        .bhanzu-prose li \u003e p { margin: 0; display: inline; }\n        .bhanzu-prose ul ul { list-style-type: circle !important; margin-top: 4px; }\n        .bhanzu-prose ul ul ul { list-style-type: square !important; }\n        /* ── Blockquote / HR / Image ── */\n        .bhanzu-prose blockquote { border-left: 3px solid #F15D22; padding: 12px 16px; background: #FFF4EF; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; margin: 18px 0; color: #4B5563; font-style: italic; }\n        .bhanzu-prose hr { height: 1px; background: #E9ECEF; border: none; margin: 32px 0; }\n        /* All images capped at container width — prevents bare \u003cimg\u003e from TipTap HTML overflowing */\n        .bhanzu-prose img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }\n        .bhanzu-prose img.md-img { border-radius: 12px; width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0; }\n        /* CLS: reserve 16:9 space for images without explicit width+height\n           so the layout doesn't jump when they load. Only applies when both\n           attributes are missing — images WITH dimensions get natural sizing. */\n        /* Reserve 16:9 space for images without explicit dimensions to prevent CLS.\n           object-fit:contain (not cover) preserves the full image without cropping —\n           portrait or square images stay fully visible, just with transparent bars. */\n        .bhanzu-prose img:not([width]):not([height]) { aspect-ratio: 16/9; width: 100%; object-fit: contain; }\n        /* ── Tables: scroll-wrapper prevents overflow, cells stay readable ── */\n        /* width:100% + display:block ensures wrapper never grows beyond its parent */\n        .bhanzu-prose .table-scroll-wrapper { overflow-x: auto; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; margin: 18px 0; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #E9ECEF; width: 100%; display: block; box-sizing: border-box; }\n        /* min-width:100% fills wrapper when content is narrow;                     */\n        /* removing fixed width:100% lets wide tables exceed the wrapper → scroll   */\n        /* ── Worksheet downloads ──────────────────────────────────────────\n           One stylesheet for all four presets, so any download block on the\n           site can be restyled here without touching a single article. */\n        .wsdl { margin: 26px 0; }\n        .wsdl a { text-decoration: none; }\n        .wsdl__grp + .wsdl__grp { margin-top: 16px; }\n        .wsdl__group { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 700; color: #6B7280; margin: 0 0 8px; letter-spacing: .02em; }\n        .wsdl__btns { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 9px; }\n        .wsdl__meta { font-size: 11px; color: #9CA3AF; font-weight: 600; }\n\n        /* button-list */\n        .wsdl--buttons .wsdl__link {\n          display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;\n          padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 8px;\n          border: 1.5px solid #F15D22; color: #F15D22;\n          background: #fff; font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 700;\n          transition: background .15s, color .15s;\n        }\n        .wsdl--buttons .wsdl__link:hover { background: #F15D22; color: #fff; }\n        .wsdl--buttons .wsdl__link:hover .wsdl__meta { color: rgba(255,255,255,.75); }\n        .wsdl__ico { font-size: 12px; }\n\n        /* thumbnail-grid */\n        .wsdl--thumbs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; }\n        .wsdl--thumbs .wsdl__link {\n          display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px;\n          border: 1px solid #E9ECEF; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden;\n          background: #fff; transition: border-color .15s, transform .15s;\n        }\n        .wsdl--thumbs .wsdl__link:hover { border-color: #F15D22; transform: translateY(-2px); }\n        .wsdl__thumb {\n          display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n          aspect-ratio: 3/4; background: #FDEEE8; overflow: hidden;\n        }\n        .wsdl__thumbimg { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }\n        .wsdl__thumbfallback { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: #F15D22; letter-spacing: .06em; }\n        .wsdl__cap { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 700; color: #0F1F3D; padding: 9px 11px 0; }\n        .wsdl--thumbs .wsdl__meta { padding: 0 11px 10px; }\n\n        /* numbered-hub */\n        .wsdl--hub { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }\n        .wsdl__n {\n          display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n          width: 46px; height: 46px; border-radius: 50%;\n          border: 1.5px solid #F15D22; color: #F15D22;\n          font-weight: 800; font-size: 15px; background: #fff;\n          transition: background .15s, color .15s;\n        }\n        .wsdl--hub .wsdl__link:hover .wsdl__n { background: #F15D22; color: #fff; }\n\n        /* inline-cta */\n        .wsdl--cta .wsdl__link {\n          display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px;\n          border: 1px solid #E9ECEF; border-radius: 10px;\n          padding: 13px 15px; background: #fff; margin-bottom: 10px;\n          transition: border-color .15s;\n        }\n        .wsdl--cta .wsdl__link:hover { border-color: #F15D22; }\n        .wsdl__ctaico {\n          flex-shrink: 0; width: 38px; height: 46px; border-radius: 5px;\n          border: 1px solid #F15D22; color: #F15D22;\n          display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n          font-size: 10px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .05em; background: #FDEEE8;\n        }\n        .wsdl__ctabody { flex: 1; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }\n        .wsdl__ctat { font-size: 14.5px; font-weight: 700; color: #0F1F3D; }\n        .wsdl__ctabtn {\n          flex-shrink: 0; padding: 8px 16px; border-radius: 7px;\n          background: #F15D22; color: #fff; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;\n        }\n        .wsdl a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #F15D22; outline-offset: 2px; }\n        @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n          .wsdl--thumbs .wsdl__link:hover { transform: none; }\n        }\n\n        .bhanzu-prose table.md-table { display: table; min-width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; margin: 0; border: none; border-radius: 0; }\n        /* Dark header ONLY for proper \u003cthead\u003e rows — grid/puzzle tables that use   */\n        /* \u003cth\u003e in \u003ctbody\u003e (e.g. magic squares) get neutral styling instead.        */\n        .bhanzu-prose table.md-table thead { background: #0F1F3D; }\n        .bhanzu-prose table.md-table thead th, .bhanzu-prose table thead th { padding: 11px 14px; text-align: left; color: #fff !important; font-weight: 700; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .04em; background: #0F1F3D !important; white-space: nowrap; }\n        /* Cover all descendants so TipTap's inline-styled \u003cspan\u003e elements don't bleed through */\n        .bhanzu-prose table thead th *, .bhanzu-prose table thead th p { color: #fff !important; background: #0F1F3D !important; margin: 0; }\n        /* th in tbody = row-header cell (e.g. first column label) — bold, no dark bg */\n        .bhanzu-prose table tbody th { padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; font-weight: 700; color: #0F1F3D !important; font-size: 13px; background: #fff !important; border-bottom: 1px solid #F3F4F6; }\n        .bhanzu-prose table tbody th *, .bhanzu-prose table tbody th p { color: #0F1F3D !important; background: #fff !important; margin: 0; }\n        .bhanzu-prose table.md-table tbody tr { border-bottom: 1px solid #F3F4F6; }\n        .bhanzu-prose table.md-table tbody tr:last-child { border: none; }\n        .bhanzu-prose table.md-table tbody tr:hover { background: #F9FAFB; }\n        .bhanzu-prose table.md-table td { padding: 10px 14px; color: #4B5563; }\n        .bhanzu-prose table.md-table td:first-child { font-weight: 700; color: #0F1F3D; }\n        /* Fallback for any unclassed table */\n        .bhanzu-prose table:not(.md-table) { display: table; min-width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; margin: 18px 0; border: 1px solid #E9ECEF; }\n        .bhanzu-prose table:not(.md-table) thead th { padding: 11px 14px; text-align: left; color: #fff !important; font-weight: 700; font-size: 11px; background: #0F1F3D !important; white-space: nowrap; }\n        .bhanzu-prose table:not(.md-table) thead th * { color: #fff !important; background: #0F1F3D !important; }\n        .bhanzu-prose table:not(.md-table) tbody th { padding: 10px 14px; font-weight: 700; color: #0F1F3D !important; background: #fff !important; }\n        .bhanzu-prose table:not(.md-table) tbody th * { color: #0F1F3D !important; background: #fff !important; }\n        .bhanzu-prose table:not(.md-table) td { padding: 10px 14px; color: #4B5563; border-bottom: 1px solid #F3F4F6; }\n        /* ── Code ── */\n        .bhanzu-prose pre.code-block { background: #1E293B; color: #E2E8F0; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; overflow-x: auto; font-family: 'Courier New',monospace; font-size: 13px; margin: 18px 0; }\n        .bhanzu-prose code.inline-code { background: #F3F4F6; color: #D9520E; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-family: 'Courier New',monospace; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; }\n        .bhanzu-prose .math-display { margin: 20px 0; text-align: center; overflow-x: auto; padding: 12px; background: #F9FAFB; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #E9ECEF; }\n        .bhanzu-prose .math-inline { font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; }\n        .bhanzu-prose del { color: #9CA3AF; text-decoration: line-through; }\n        /* ── Accordion / Collapsible FAQ ── */\n        .bhanzu-prose details.md-accordion { border: 1px solid #E9ECEF; border-radius: 10px; margin: 10px 0; overflow: hidden; }\n        .bhanzu-prose details.md-accordion summary.md-accordion-summary { padding: 14px 18px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; color: #0F1F3D; cursor: pointer; background: #F9FAFB; list-style: none; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; }\n        .bhanzu-prose details.md-accordion summary.md-accordion-summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }\n        .bhanzu-prose details.md-accordion summary.md-accordion-summary::after { content: '+'; font-size: 18px; color: #F15D22; transition: transform 0.2s; }\n        .bhanzu-prose details.md-accordion[open] summary.md-accordion-summary::after { content: '−'; }\n        .bhanzu-prose details.md-accordion .md-accordion-body { padding: 14px 18px; font-size: 15px; color: #4B5563; line-height: 1.75; border-top: 1px solid #E9ECEF; }\n        /* ── Mobile layout ── */\n        @media (max-width: 1100px) {\n          /* Collapse 3-col grid to single-column flex stack */\n          .page-grid {\n            display: flex !important;\n            flex-direction: column !important;\n            padding: 16px 20px !important;\n            gap: 0 !important;\n          }\n          /* Every direct flex child must fill the full width */\n          .page-article-header,\n          .page-article-body,\n          .page-sidebar-aside {\n            width: 100% !important;\n            box-sizing: border-box !important;\n            min-width: 0 !important;\n          }\n          /* Remove the cross-axis start alignment that shrinks sidebar on mobile */\n          .page-sidebar-aside {\n            position: static !important;\n            align-self: stretch !important;\n            top: auto !important;\n          }\n          /* Article body: let content overflow horizontally inside scroll wrappers\n             instead of being hard-clipped by the parent */\n          .page-article-body {\n            overflow: visible !important;\n            padding-top: 20px !important;\n          }\n          /* TOC hidden on tablet/mobile */\n          .page-toc-aside { display: none !important; }\n          /* Table scroll wrapper capped to viewport */\n          .bhanzu-prose .table-scroll-wrapper { max-width: calc(100vw - 40px); }\n        }\n        @media (max-width: 640px) {\n          .page-grid { padding: 12px 16px !important; }\n          .bhanzu-prose .table-scroll-wrapper { max-width: calc(100vw - 32px); }\n          /* Tighter prose font on small phones */\n          .bhanzu-prose p, .bhanzu-prose li { font-size: 14px; }\n          .bhanzu-prose h2 { font-size: 18px; }\n          .bhanzu-prose h3 { font-size: 15px; }\n        }\n      "])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1c:[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"children\":\"$2b\"}]\n1d:[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"children\":\"\\n          @media (max-width: 1100px) {\\n            .page-root { padding-bottom: var(--mobile-lead-bar-height, 64px); }\\n          }\\n        \"}]\n2c:Tcb1,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"/* ============================================================\r\n   BLOG POST STYLES  —  edit any value and click Save\r\n   Tip: colour = color, size in px, spacing in px\r\n   ============================================================ */\r\n\r\n/* ------ PAGE TITLE (the big H1 at the top) ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose h1 { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 900; color: #0F1F3D; margin: 0 0 16px; line-height: 1.2; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ SECTION HEADING (H2 — used for major sections) ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose h2 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 800; color: #0F1F3D; margin: 40px 0 12px; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ SUB-HEADING (H3 — used inside sections) ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose h3 { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; color: #0F1F3D; margin: 24px 0 10px; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ SMALL HEADING (H4) ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose h4 { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: #0F1F3D; margin: 18px 0 8px; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ BODY TEXT (regular paragraphs) ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose p { font-size: 15px; color: #4B5563; margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.85; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ BOLD TEXT ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose strong { color: #0F1F3D; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ ITALIC TEXT ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose em { font-style: italic; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ LINKS (clickable text) ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose a { color: #F15D22; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px dotted rgba(255,107,43,.4); }\r\n.bhanzu-prose a:hover { border-bottom-style: solid; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ BULLET LISTS and NUMBERED LISTS ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose ul, .bhanzu-prose ol { padding-left: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; color: #4B5563; }\r\n.bhanzu-prose li { margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 15px; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ PULL QUOTE / BLOCKQUOTE (the indented callout box) ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose blockquote { border-left: 3px solid #F15D22; padding: 12px 16px; background: #FFF4EF; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; margin: 18px 0; color: #4B5563; font-style: italic; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ HORIZONTAL DIVIDER LINE (---) ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose hr { height: 1px; background: #E9ECEF; border: none; margin: 32px 0; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ IMAGES ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose img { border-radius: 12px; width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ TABLES ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose table { width: 100%; table-layout: fixed; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 18px 0; font-size: 13px; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid #E9ECEF; }\r\n.bhanzu-prose thead { background: #0F1F3D; } /* table header row background */\r\n.bhanzu-prose th { padding: 11px 14px; color: #fff !important; font-weight: 700; font-size: 11px; text-align: left; letter-spacing: .04em; background: #0F1F3D !important; }\r\n.bhanzu-prose tbody tr { border-bottom: 1px solid #F3F4F6; }\r\n.bhanzu-prose tbody tr:hover { background: #F9FAFB; } /* row highlight on hover */\r\n.bhanzu-prose td { padding: 10px 14px; color: #4B5563; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ CODE BLOCK (multi-line code snippet) ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose pre { background: #1E293B; color: #E2E8F0; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; overflow-x: auto; font-family: monospace; font-size: 13px; margin: 18px 0; }\r\n\r\n/* ------ INLINE CODE (short code inside a sentence) ------ */\r\n.bhanzu-prose code { background: #F3F4F6; color: #D9520E; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-family: monospace; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; }"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1e:[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$2c\"}}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2d:I[78858,[\"https://blog.bhanzu.com/_next/static/chunks/289c98a5c27dd4bb.js\",\"https://blog.bhanzu.com/_next/static/chunks/fa907f97ab85c687.js\",\"https://blog.bhanzu.com/_next/static/chunks/e0da408efd949077.js\"],\"default\"]\n2e:I[28472,[\"https://blog.bhanzu.com/_next/static/chunks/289c98a5c27dd4bb.js\",\"https://blog.bhanzu.com/_next/static/chunks/fa907f97ab85c687.js\",\"https://blog.bhanzu.com/_next/static/chunks/e0da408efd949077.js\"],\"default\"]\n35:I[59011,[\"https://blog.bhanzu.com/_next/static/chunks/289c98a5c27dd4bb.js\",\"https://blog.bhanzu.com/_next/static/chunks/fa907f97ab85c687.js\",\"https://blog.bhanzu.com/_next/static/chunks/e0da408efd949077.js\"],\"DemoCard\"]\n22:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"marginTop\":\"20px\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2d\",null,{\"title\":\"What is Meter — Definition, Conversion \u0026 Examples in Math\",\"url\":\"https://bhanzu.com/math/terms/meter\"}]}]\n23:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"marginTop\":\"20px\",\"paddingTop\":\"16px\",\"borderTop\":\"1px solid #E9ECEF\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"12px\",\"fontWeight\":700,\"color\":\"#0F1F3D\",\"marginBottom\":\"8px\"},\"children\":\"Was this helpful?\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"display\":\"flex\",\"gap\":\"9px\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2e\",null,{}]}]]}]\n2f:T3692,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003cp\u003eA \u003cstrong\u003emeter\u003c/strong\u003e is the worldwide standard unit of length. From shoe size to running track to highway distance, the meter (or its multiples and submultiples) is how most of the world measures.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"the-formal-definition\"\u003eThe Formal Definition\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003emeter\u003c/strong\u003e (or \u003cstrong\u003emetre\u003c/strong\u003e in British spelling) is the SI base unit of length. Since $1983$, it has been formally defined as:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ethe length of the path travelled by light in a vacuum during a time interval of $\\dfrac{1}{299{,}792{,}458}$ of a second.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn simpler terms: the meter is defined through the speed of light, which is a universal constant. This definition guarantees that one meter in Paris equals one meter in Mumbai equals one meter on Mars — the same physical length, anywhere.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEarlier definitions (1791) had the meter as one ten-millionth of the distance from the equator to the North Pole along the meridian through Paris. By 1889 it became the length of a platinum-iridium bar held in Sèvres, France. The 1983 redefinition tied it to a universal constant of nature so that the unit could not drift over time.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eQuick reference.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSymbol:\u003c/strong\u003e m (meter / metre).\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSI base unit for:\u003c/strong\u003e length.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEquivalents:\u003c/strong\u003e $1$ m $= 100$ cm $= 1000$ mm $= 0.001$ km.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eImperial:\u003c/strong\u003e $1$ m $\\approx 3.281$ feet $\\approx 39.37$ inches $\\approx 1.094$ yards.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGrade introduced:\u003c/strong\u003e CCSS-M \u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://4.MD\" class=\"md-link\"\u003e4.MD\u003c/a\u003e.A.1 (units of measurement); NCERT Class 5 Chapter — Tenths and Hundredths / Class 6 Mensuration.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"the-metric-length-ladder-prefixes-and-powers-of-10\"\u003eThe Metric Length Ladder — Prefixes and Powers of 10\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eEvery metric length unit is a power of $10$ times the meter. The seven most-used prefixes around the meter:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"table-scroll-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ctable style=\"min-width: 75px;\" class=\"md-table\"\u003e\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eUnit\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eSymbol\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eIn meters\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eKilometer\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003ekm\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$1{,}000$ m $= 10^{3}$ m\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eHectometer\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003ehm\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$100$ m $= 10^{2}$ m\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eDecameter\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003edam\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$10$ m\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMeter\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003em\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e$1$ m\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eDecimeter\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003edm\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$0.1$ m $= 10^{-1}$ m\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eCentimeter\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003ecm\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$0.01$ m $= 10^{-2}$ m\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eMillimeter\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003emm\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$0.001$ m $= 10^{-3}$ m\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo convert between units, move the decimal point — one place per \"step\" on the ladder. Going down the ladder (m $\\to$ cm $\\to$ mm) means dividing by $10$ each time; going up (m $\\to$ km) means dividing by larger powers.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eA useful rule of thumb: km $\\to$ m $\\to$ cm $\\to$ mm — each arrow is a $\\times 1000$ then $\\times 100$ then $\\times 10$ if you spell out the gaps with dam, hm, dm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"meter-to-imperial-the-most-used-conversions\"\u003eMeter to Imperial — The Most-Used Conversions\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"table-scroll-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ctable style=\"min-width: 100px;\" class=\"md-table\"\u003e\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eMeter\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eFeet\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eInches\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003eYards\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$1$ m\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$3.281$ ft\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$39.37$ in\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$1.094$ yd\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$5$ m\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$16.40$ ft\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$196.85$ in\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$5.47$ yd\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$10$ m\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$32.81$ ft\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$393.70$ in\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$10.94$ yd\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$100$ m\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$328.08$ ft\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$3{,}937.01$ in\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$109.36$ yd\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$1$ km\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$3{,}280.84$ ft\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e—\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\"\u003e\u003cp style=\"text-align: center;\"\u003e$1{,}093.61$ yd\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003eA mile is $1{,}609.34$ m. A marathon ($42.195$ km) is exactly $26.2$ miles. A foot is exactly $0.3048$ m (this is a definition, not an approximation — adopted in $1959$ by both the US and UK).\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"three-worked-examples-of-meter-quick-standard-stretch\"\u003eThree Worked Examples of Meter — Quick, Standard, Stretch\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eQuick.\u003c/strong\u003e Convert $3.5$ m to centimetres.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e$1$ m $= 100$ cm, so $3.5$ m $= 3.5 \\times 100 = 350$ cm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFinal answer:\u003c/strong\u003e $350$ cm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStandard (Wrong Path First — Where Conversions Slip).\u003c/strong\u003e A field is $250$ m long. Express this in kilometres.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eThe wrong path.\u003c/em\u003e A student multiplies: $250 \\times 1000 = 250{,}000$ km.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe flaw: km is the \u003cem\u003elarger\u003c/em\u003e unit. Going from a smaller unit (m) to a larger unit (km), you \u003cem\u003edivide\u003c/em\u003e, not multiply. Multiplying by $1000$ gives a number that's a million times too big.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eThe rescue.\u003c/em\u003e $1$ km $= 1000$ m, so $1$ m $= \\dfrac{1}{1000}$ km. Therefore:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e$$250 \\text{ m} = \\frac{250}{1000} \\text{ km} = 0.25 \\text{ km}.$$\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFinal answer:\u003c/strong\u003e $0.25$ km.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe lesson — \u003cstrong\u003egoing from a smaller unit to a larger one, divide; going from a larger to a smaller, multiply.\u003c/strong\u003e The direction of conversion decides the operation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStretch.\u003c/strong\u003e A swimming pool is $50$ m long and $25$ m wide. Express the perimeter in (a) meters, (b) feet, and (c) yards. Round to two decimal places.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e(a) Perimeter $= 2(l + b) = 2(50 + 25) = 150$ m.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e(b) $1$ m $\\approx 3.281$ ft, so $150 \\times 3.281 \\approx 492.15$ ft.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e(c) $1$ m $\\approx 1.094$ yd, so $150 \\times 1.094 \\approx 164.10$ yd.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFinal answer:\u003c/strong\u003e (a) $150$ m, (b) $\\approx 492.15$ ft, (c) $\\approx 164.10$ yd.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis is the version of meter conversion problem that shows up in NCERT Class 6 mensuration and in any U.S. textbook covering imperial-metric conversion under CCSS-M \u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"http://4.MD\" class=\"md-link\"\u003e4.MD\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"where-the-meter-appears-beyond-the-tape-measure\"\u003eWhere the Meter Appears — Beyond the Tape Measure\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe meter is used everywhere length matters:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSports.\u003c/strong\u003e Olympic events are run in $100$-m, $200$-m, $400$-m, and $1500$-m distances. A track lane is exactly $1.22$ m wide. A football (soccer) field is $100$–$110$ m long.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConstruction.\u003c/strong\u003e Floor plans, beam lengths, room dimensions — almost every country except the U.S. and Liberia uses metres directly. (U.S. construction still uses feet and inches.)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eScientific work.\u003c/strong\u003e Wavelengths of light (hundreds of nanometres), DNA strands (about $2$ nm wide), distances between Earth and the Sun ($1.496 \\times 10^{11}$ m) — every length-based measurement in modern science is rooted in the meter.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCartography.\u003c/strong\u003e A topographic map's contour lines are spaced in metres of elevation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGPS.\u003c/strong\u003e A typical civilian GPS receiver locates you to within $5$–$10$ meters globally.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe meter was created during the French Revolution by a commission of scientists including \u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://mathshistory.st-andrews.ac.uk/Biographies/Laplace/\" class=\"md-link\"\u003ePierre-Simon Laplace (1749–1827, France)\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://mathshistory.st-andrews.ac.uk/Biographies/Lagrange/\" class=\"md-link\"\u003eJoseph-Louis Lagrange (1736–1813, Italy/France)\u003c/a\u003e — the goal was a unit \"for all people, for all time\" rooted in nature rather than in the size of one king's foot. The metric system spread globally over the next $200$ years; by $2026$, every country except the United States, Liberia, and Myanmar uses it as the official measurement system.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"tripping-points-to-avoid-in-meter\"\u003eTripping Points to Avoid In Meter\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"mistake-1-multiplying-when-you-should-divide-or-vice-versa\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMistake 1: Multiplying when you should divide (or vice versa)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere it slips in:\u003c/strong\u003e Converting metres to kilometres by multiplying.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDon't do this:\u003c/strong\u003e Use the same operation regardless of direction.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe correct way:\u003c/strong\u003e Smaller unit $\\to$ larger unit: divide. Larger unit $\\to$ smaller unit: multiply. $250$ m $= 0.25$ km, not $250{,}000$ km.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"mistake-2-mixing-metric-and-imperial-units-in-one-calculation\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMistake 2: Mixing metric and imperial units in one calculation\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere it slips in:\u003c/strong\u003e Adding $3$ m and $2$ ft directly.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDon't do this:\u003c/strong\u003e Treat metric and imperial units as interchangeable.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe correct way:\u003c/strong\u003e Convert to a single system first. $2$ ft $\\approx 0.61$ m, so $3 + 0.61 = 3.61$ m. Or convert $3$ m to feet first.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3 id=\"mistake-3-confusing-meter-length-with-meter-a-measuring-device\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMistake 3: Confusing meter (length) with meter (a measuring device)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere it slips in:\u003c/strong\u003e \"I bought a flow meter — is it $1$ m long?\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDon't do this:\u003c/strong\u003e Confuse the unit with the instrument.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe correct way:\u003c/strong\u003e The \u003cem\u003emeter\u003c/em\u003e (unit) is a length. A \u003cem\u003emeter\u003c/em\u003e (device — gas meter, parking meter, ammeter) is an instrument that measures something. The two share a name but mean different things.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eA real-world version of the mistake.\u003c/strong\u003e The \u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-climate-orbiter/\" class=\"md-link\"\u003eMars Climate Orbiter\u003c/a\u003e was lost in $1999$ because two engineering teams worked in different unit systems — one in pound-seconds (imperial), the other in newton-seconds (SI). The unit mismatch was never caught. The lesson is the same as the lesson on the bathroom scale: numbers without consistent units are dangerous.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"conclusion\"\u003eConclusion\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003emeter\u003c/strong\u003e (m) is the SI base unit of length.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIt equals $100$ cm, $1000$ mm, and $0.001$ km — every metric length unit is a power of $10$ from the meter.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e$1$ m $\\approx 3.281$ feet; $1$ ft $= 0.3048$ m exactly.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDefined since $1983$ via the speed of light: the distance light travels in $1/299{,}792{,}458$ of a second.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eMultiply when converting to a smaller unit, divide when converting to a larger one — the most common mistake reverses these.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2 id=\"quick-self-check-three-conversions\"\u003eQuick Self-Check — Three Conversions\u003c/h2\u003e\u003col\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eConvert $4.5$ km to meters.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eConvert $750$ cm to meters.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eConvert $10$ m to feet (use $1$ m $\\approx 3.281$ ft).\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf problem 2 gave $75{,}000$ m, return to Mistake 1 above — you multiplied when you should have divided.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWant a live Bhanzu trainer to walk your child through unit conversion and metric system fluency? \u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://bhanzu.com/book-demo-lp?utm_source=blog\u0026amp;utm_medium=article\u0026amp;utm_campaign=what-is-meter#book-demo\" class=\"md-link\"\u003eBook a free demo class\u003c/a\u003e — online globally.\u003c/p\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"24:[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"page-article-body\",\"style\":{\"gridColumn\":2,\"gridRow\":2,\"minWidth\":0,\"paddingTop\":\"24px\",\"overflow\":\"hidden\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bhanzu-prose\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$2f\"}}],\"$L30\",\"$L31\",\"$L32\",\"$L33\",\"$L34\"]}]\n25:[\"$\",\"aside\",null,{\"className\":\"page-sidebar-aside\",\"style\":{\"gridColumn\":3,\"gridRow\":\"1 / span 2\",\"position\":\"sticky\",\"top\":\"120px\",\"alignSelf\":\"start\",\"display\":\"flex\",\"flexDirection\":\"column\",\"gap\":\"14px\",\"zIndex\":1},\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L35\",\"7\",{\"cfg\":{\"eyebrow\":\"Math · UKG to Grade 9\",\"title\":\"Looking for a personal math tutor for your child?\",\"subtitle\":\"Live 1:6 classes with India's fastest human calculator\",\"emoji\":\"👨‍🏫👧\",\"cta_text\":\"Book FREE Demo Lesson\",\"cta_type\":\"popup\",\"cta_url\":\"https://bhanzu.com/#bookslot\",\"note\":\"✓ Free · ✓ Live class · ✓ No card needed\",\"popup_embed\":\"https://bhanzu.com/embeddable-demo-form?utm_source=article\"}}]],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"border\":\"1px solid #E9ECEF\",\"borderRadius\":\"14px\",\"padding\":\"16px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"10px\",\"fontWeight\":800,\"letterSpacing\":\".12em\",\"textTransform\":\"uppercase\",\"color\":\"#ADB5BD\",\"marginBottom\":\"10px\"},\"children\":\"Topics\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"display\":\"flex\",\"flexWrap\":\"wrap\",\"gap\":\"6px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",\"Math Terms\",{\"href\":\"/tag/math-terms\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"#FFF4EF\",\"color\":\"#F15D22\",\"borderRadius\":\"20px\",\"padding\":\"3px 10px\",\"fontSize\":\"11px\",\"fontWeight\":700,\"border\":\"1px solid rgba(241,93,34,0.2)\",\"textDecoration\":\"none\"},\"children\":[\"#\",\"Math Terms\"]}]]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"36:I[87339,[\"https://blog.bhanzu.com/_next/static/chunks/289c98a5c27dd4bb.js\",\"https://blog.bhanzu.com/_next/static/chunks/fa907f97ab85c687.js\",\"https://blog.bhanzu.com/_next/static/chunks/e0da408efd949077.js\"],\"default\"]\n:HL[\"https://static.bhanzu.com/blog-images/geometry-types-of-quadrilaterals/1784800838142-c8e01b21.webp\",\"image\"]\n30:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"margin\":\"32px 0\",\"borderRadius\":\"14px\",\"overflow\":\"hidden\",\"border\":\"1px solid #E9ECEF\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://bhanzu.com/embeddable-demo-form?utm_source=article-image-cta\",\"style\":{\"display\":\"block\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://static.bhanzu.com/blog-images/geometry-types-of-quadrilaterals/1784800838142-c8e01b21.webp\",\"alt\":\"Book a Free Demo\",\"style\":{\"width\":\"100%\",\"height\":\"auto\",\"display\":\"block\"}}]}]}]\n31:[\"$\",\"$L36\",null,{}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"32:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"marginTop\":\"36px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"20px\",\"fontWeight\":800,\"color\":\"#0F1F3D\",\"marginBottom\":\"16px\"},\"children\":\"Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"bhanzu-prose\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"md-accordion\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-summary\",\"children\":\"What is a meter in math?\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-body\",\"children\":\"The SI base unit of length, equal to $100$ centimetres or about $3.28$ feet.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"md-accordion\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-summary\",\"children\":\"How is the meter defined?\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-body\",\"children\":\"As the length light travels in vacuum in $1/299{,}792{,}458$ of a second.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"md-accordion\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-summary\",\"children\":\"How many centimetres are in $1$ meter?\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-body\",\"children\":\"$$100$ centimetres.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"md-accordion\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-summary\",\"children\":\"How many feet are in $1$ meter?\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-body\",\"children\":\"Approximately $3.281$ feet, or exactly $\\\\dfrac{1}{0.3048}$ feet (since $1$ ft $= 0.3048$ m).\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"md-accordion\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-summary\",\"children\":\"How many meters are in $1$ kilometre?\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-body\",\"children\":\"$$1{,}000$ meters.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"md-accordion\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-summary\",\"children\":\"What's the difference between \\\"meter\\\" and \\\"metre\\\"?\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-body\",\"children\":\"Spelling only. American English uses \\\"meter\\\"; British and most other English uses \\\"metre.\\\" They refer to the same unit.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"md-accordion\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-summary\",\"children\":\"Who invented the meter?\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"md-accordion-body\",\"children\":\"The French Academy of Sciences proposed it in $1791$ as a unit \\\"for all people, for all time.\\\" It became the international standard with the Metric Convention of $1875$.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"33:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"marginTop\":\"36px\",\"border\":\"1px solid #E9ECEF\",\"borderRadius\":\"16px\",\"padding\":\"20px\",\"background\":\"#FAFAFA\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"10px\",\"fontWeight\":800,\"letterSpacing\":\".1em\",\"textTransform\":\"uppercase\",\"color\":\"#F15D22\",\"marginBottom\":\"14px\"},\"children\":\"✍️ Written By\"}],[[\"$\",\"div\",\"Bhanzu Team\",{\"style\":{\"display\":\"flex\",\"gap\":\"14px\",\"alignItems\":\"flex-start\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"width\":\"52px\",\"height\":\"52px\",\"borderRadius\":\"50%\",\"flexShrink\":0,\"display\":\"flex\",\"alignItems\":\"center\",\"justifyContent\":\"center\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\",\"fontWeight\":800,\"color\":\"#fff\",\"background\":\"linear-gradient(135deg,#F15D22,#FFB347)\",\"border\":\"2px solid #fff\"},\"children\":\"BT\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"minWidth\":0,\"flex\":1},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/authors/bhanzu-team\",\"style\":{\"fontFamily\":\"'Quicksand','Quicksand Fallback',sans-serif\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\",\"fontWeight\":800,\"color\":\"#F15D22\",\"marginBottom\":\"2px\",\"textDecoration\":\"none\",\"display\":\"block\"},\"children\":\"Bhanzu Team\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"12px\",\"color\":\"#6B7280\",\"marginBottom\":\"6px\"},\"children\":\"Content Creator and Editor\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"fontSize\":\"13px\",\"color\":\"#4B5563\",\"lineHeight\":1.65},\"children\":\"Bhanzu’s editorial team, known as Team Bhanzu, is made up of experienced educators, curriculum experts, content strategists, and fact-checkers dedicated to making math simple and engaging for learners worldwide. Every article and resource is carefully researched, thoughtfully structured, and rigorously reviewed to ensure accuracy, clarity, and real-world relevance.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe understand that building strong math foundations can raise questions for 